From here I'll submit stage=result with the complete design. Keep it concise and concrete, covering the following:

1. Input interface (CSV/TSV id,name,smiles) + embedded demo dataset (~15 molecules and SMILES + control values).
2. Main Route B (pure standard-library implementation) + Route A (RDKit) 1:1 mapping table + portability notes.
3. Property modules: core graph-derived ones + optional logP (Wildman–Crippen) / TPSA (Ertl), made explicit that they are approximate values.
4. QC/controls: MW cross-check, parse rate ≥95%, exclusion log, deduplication via canonical SMILES, traceability; explain how each control detects parser failures (unbalanced parentheses, invalid ring indices, unsupported stereo descriptors).
5. Analysis plan: quartiles, Spearman (rank transform + statistics.correlation), Rule of Five, IQR 1.5× outliers, text histograms without matplotlib.
Feasibility assessment in this environment.

Include the demo dataset list with SMILES:
- aspirin: CC(=O)Oc1ccccc1C(=O)O — control 180.16
- caffeine: Cn1cnc2c1c(=O)n(c(=O)n2C)C — 194.19
- ethanol: CCO — 46.07
